            <ArticleTitle>Understanding the pathogenesis of vascular calcification: timing is everything.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1316-1318</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0085-2538(17)30552-5</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.kint.2017.07.020</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A number of histologic changes are associated with the medial arterial calcification that occurs in chronic kidney disease, leading to several different hypotheses concerning the underlying mechanism. Careful timing of these changes in relation to the onset of the calcification, as reported in this issue of the journal, can shed light on which changes are pathogenic as opposed to secondary in reaction to the calcification.</AbstractText>
